{:edb/db-before-t 2719 :edb/db-after-t 2720 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536032 50 #inst "2026-10-09T13:17:57.349Z" 13194139536032 true] [17592186198335 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380171 13194139536032 true] [17592186198335 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380178 13194139536032 true] [17592186198335 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380185 13194139536032 true] [17592186198336 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380157 13194139536032 true] [17592186198336 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380164 13194139536032 true] [17592186380157 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380158 13194139536032 true] [17592186380157 1089 "q-163017" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380157 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536032 true] [17592186380157 1100 "Consider a thin rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $0\\le x\\le 1$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)=x-{x}^{3}.$ Given that the rod's mass is $\\frac{1}{4}$ units, what is the $x$-coordinate of its center of mass?" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380157 1113 #uuid "fb9ee0e9-a4ee-5ca7-94fc-a842143f8b71" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380157 1145 "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\,x\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=x-{x}^{3},\\,a=0,\\,b=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot (x-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}-{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{2}{15})}{(\\frac{1}{4})}=\\frac{8}{15}.\n$$" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380159 13194139536032 true] [17592186380158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380160 13194139536032 true] [17592186380158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380161 13194139536032 true] [17592186380158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380162 13194139536032 true] [17592186380158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380163 13194139536032 true] [17592186380158 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536032 true] [17592186380158 1041 "selection" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380158 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380163 13194139536032 true] [17592186380158 1110 #uuid "cee4dfca-811d-5bc3-8859-8aa779d9c84e" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380159 1034 "\\frac{5}{12}" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380159 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536032 true] [17592186380159 1111 #uuid "1798dc95-a88b-5830-a37c-aa39a3cf36b5" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380160 1034 "\\frac{4}{5}" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380160 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536032 true] [17592186380160 1111 #uuid "099868d7-54d2-59e4-aa2b-31c18cda28df" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380161 1034 "\\frac{2}{9}" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380161 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536032 true] [17592186380161 1111 #uuid "247e8346-c664-5d32-9ab1-dbb3837116cd" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380162 1034 "\\frac{7}{10}" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380162 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536032 true] [17592186380162 1111 #uuid "400216c3-4c32-5c45-94f6-06d884c1dc9b" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380163 1034 "\\frac{8}{15}" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380163 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536032 true] [17592186380163 1111 #uuid "70a37107-9eec-5f7a-a71d-1759942f9ae4" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380164 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380165 13194139536032 true] [17592186380164 1089 "q-163026" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380164 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536032 true] [17592186380164 1100 "Consider a thin rod along the $x$-axis over the interval $0\\le x\\le 2$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)=8-{x}^{3}.$ Find the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass of the rod." 13194139536032 true] [17592186380164 1113 #uuid "ce12c155-0b0c-54e7-ab6e-07055f488a20" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380164 1145 "The center of mass of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\,x\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=8-{x}^{3},\\,a=0,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nSo, the mass of the rod is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}8-{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[8x-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =8\\cdot 2-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nand the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot (8-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}8x-{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[4{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 4-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 32 \\\\  & =\\frac{48}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{48}{5})}{12}=\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380165 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380166 13194139536032 true] [17592186380165 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380167 13194139536032 true] [17592186380165 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380168 13194139536032 true] [17592186380165 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380169 13194139536032 true] [17592186380165 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380170 13194139536032 true] [17592186380165 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536032 true] [17592186380165 1041 "selection" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380165 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380166 13194139536032 true] [17592186380165 1110 #uuid "9d67c41c-767b-560b-aa4e-febb80b1d18c" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380166 1034 "\\frac{4}{5}" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380166 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536032 true] [17592186380166 1111 #uuid "d20899eb-a545-5ee2-a4ac-defea1eb79ec" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380167 1034 "\\frac{8}{9}" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380167 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536032 true] [17592186380167 1111 #uuid "cc02c24e-c077-5129-a1c9-65a20de7ef55" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380168 1034 "\\frac{4}{3}" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380168 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536032 true] [17592186380168 1111 #uuid "9888a884-ee81-5b94-9a57-88afe4ea6f2c" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380169 1034 "\\frac{7}{6}" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380169 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536032 true] [17592186380169 1111 #uuid "a09a5ed1-8735-55ec-b8d2-33fa6c23fb93" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380170 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380170 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536032 true] [17592186380170 1111 #uuid "646fe3c6-3b34-5019-9b0b-11fcd6417a12" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380171 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380172 13194139536032 true] [17592186380171 1089 "q-163037" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380171 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536032 true] [17592186380171 1100 "A thin rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)=\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}},$ measured in $\\text{kg/m},$ is placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $1\\le x\\le 4,$ where $x$ is measured in meters. Find the moment of the rod about the origin." 13194139536032 true] [17592186380171 1113 #uuid "433423a2-b43c-52b3-9c92-28839eb23526" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380171 1145 "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}},\\,a=1,\\,b=4.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}x\\cdot \\frac{4}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{4}{x}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{4}{4}-\\frac{4}{1}) \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $3\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380173 13194139536032 true] [17592186380172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380174 13194139536032 true] [17592186380172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380175 13194139536032 true] [17592186380172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380176 13194139536032 true] [17592186380172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380177 13194139536032 true] [17592186380172 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536032 true] [17592186380172 1041 "selection" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380172 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380175 13194139536032 true] [17592186380172 1110 #uuid "23daab5d-8457-5170-9548-0029ba645aac" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380173 1034 "9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380173 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536032 true] [17592186380173 1111 #uuid "6b16454b-b7c2-57ea-b38e-53b69d656c21" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380174 1034 "4.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380174 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536032 true] [17592186380174 1111 #uuid "313396c5-3ebb-5100-9ce7-f6cc6ac62628" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380175 1034 "3\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380175 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536032 true] [17592186380175 1111 #uuid "df072a7c-023e-558a-a11f-cd3aa65723bb" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380176 1034 "6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380176 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536032 true] [17592186380176 1111 #uuid "2f0aaab3-2d05-5d9f-9c4d-9b0eaa062b10" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380177 1034 "2.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380177 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536032 true] [17592186380177 1111 #uuid "17e77b55-adb9-52d8-b3f7-6f0c5ac01682" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380178 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380179 13194139536032 true] [17592186380178 1089 "q-163086" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380178 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536032 true] [17592186380178 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/assets/32500120ed36acde90f5b27c44a6cf45f2d4766bacb5eb097debc0cd7117f27f.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{kg/m}.$ Find the moment of the rod about the origin." 13194139536032 true] [17592186380178 1113 #uuid "ca4c8b56-011b-565a-8401-27eb069a9443" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380178 1145 "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}},\\,a=1,\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\cdot \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{2}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380179 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380180 13194139536032 true] [17592186380179 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380181 13194139536032 true] [17592186380179 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380182 13194139536032 true] [17592186380179 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380183 13194139536032 true] [17592186380179 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380184 13194139536032 true] [17592186380179 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536032 true] [17592186380179 1041 "selection" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380179 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380181 13194139536032 true] [17592186380179 1110 #uuid "88c7cab0-5d8e-5c39-ad80-3184a475ab75" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380180 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380180 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536032 true] [17592186380180 1111 #uuid "655d1ea2-8a07-59d5-af93-8d052d77d4e4" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380181 1034 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380181 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536032 true] [17592186380181 1111 #uuid "ca4440cf-49d9-57d9-abef-1a136176bcdf" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380182 1034 "3\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380182 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536032 true] [17592186380182 1111 #uuid "9f3f0d29-3e3b-559b-bf72-6a308797d4cb" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380183 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380183 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536032 true] [17592186380183 1111 #uuid "4e226d91-9f43-5002-b740-667d217285de" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380184 1034 "2\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380184 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536032 true] [17592186380184 1111 #uuid "d72d2ec8-14d5-506f-81b3-ed8f97863f8b" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380185 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380186 13194139536032 true] [17592186380185 1089 "q-163087" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380185 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536032 true] [17592186380185 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/assets/32500120ed36acde90f5b27c44a6cf45f2d4766bacb5eb097debc0cd7117f27f.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)={x}^{2}-x\\,\\text{kg/m}.$ Find the moment of the rod about the origin." 13194139536032 true] [17592186380185 1113 #uuid "154a88f6-8666-5c12-8294-951388b62b91" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380185 1145 "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)={x}^{2}-x,\\,a=1,\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\cdot ({x}^{2}-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{3}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3})-(\\frac{{1}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{1}^{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{34}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $\\frac{34}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380187 13194139536032 true] [17592186380186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380188 13194139536032 true] [17592186380186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380189 13194139536032 true] [17592186380186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380190 13194139536032 true] [17592186380186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380191 13194139536032 true] [17592186380186 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536032 true] [17592186380186 1041 "selection" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380186 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380187 13194139536032 true] [17592186380186 1110 #uuid "3f930f9c-aa1a-5d68-9514-6bd0cc83defe" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380187 1034 "\\frac{34}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380187 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536032 true] [17592186380187 1111 #uuid "639aba2d-4d44-5df5-a022-794eb7246058" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380188 1034 "\\frac{43}{9}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380188 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536032 true] [17592186380188 1111 #uuid "2ba065d1-b0ab-5e25-a362-0045c82160ee" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380189 1034 "\\frac{25}{6}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380189 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536032 true] [17592186380189 1111 #uuid "e5d19674-2d97-5ca4-89a2-9842ec8983b0" 13194139536032 true] [17592186380190 1034 "11\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" 13194139536032 true] [17592186